# <product> <low>-<high> — one contiguous port band per product on this machine,
# every band above Linux's ephemeral range (which ends at 60999). A copy of the
# starter template reserves its band here: scripts/copy-template.sh refuses a
# band that overlaps an entry and appends the new product's reservation itself,
# under a lock. Entries cover this machine's other projects too, so a copy can
# never take a band another product already holds. Lines are exactly
# "<name> <low>-<high>" in ASCII — a malformed line refuses the copy.
